**Chart Your Journey at Secretariat**
From a collaborative culture to teammates who will always be by your side, find a career that will grow with you. Deliver your impact at Secretariat.


Secretariat professionals are trusted in the highest-stakes legal, risk, and regulatory matters around the world.


When you join Secretariat, you become part of a rapidly growing elite team of bright minds and passionate problem-solvers. Your skills and expertise will be utilised on day one – working with the world’s most renowned law firms, leading corporations, and influential institutions to answer complex questions that shape critical financial, economic, and strategic business decisions.


Our globally integrated teams are united by the ambition, energy, and commitment they bring to every challenge. We inspire and empower an open, collaborative culture that embraces ongoing professional development, recognition, diversity, and – most importantly – you.


Make your impact at Secretariat.


**About Our Construction Quantum Team**
Whether it’s to prevent or prepare for potential project complications before they begin, manage and mitigate risk on an ongoing project, or resolve disputes rooted in issues from the past, Secretariat experts understand the complexities that can result in delays and costs. Our quantity surveyors, engineers, forensic accountants, project managers, architects, schedulers, and industry specialists are experts in the valuation of construction works of all types and have experience handling projects in every corner of the world.


**Responsibilities**
We are looking for an ambitious, self-motivated, and proactive team player to join our growing team of highly experienced quantity surveying experts, based in our Dubai office.


The ideal candidate will be a quantity surveying professional with 5- 10 years’ experience of working on construction and engineering projects with either a consultant, contractor, or client. Ideally, previous experience of working with an Expert Witness and taking responsibility for leading streams of work and drafting sections of reports or appendices is preferred.


Your primary duties as a Manager, will be to provide support to testifying Expert Witnesses, with a long-term view of one day becoming a testifying expert in your own right.


**Role**
Some of the tasks you will fulfil in this role before you progress your career with us, will be as follows:



* Supporting world-renowned Quantum experts in dispute resolution, litigation support and expert witness evidence;
* Performing data research, management and analysis, and assisting in drafting sections of expert reports;
* Reviewing documentation (e.g. drawings, specifications, reports, estimates, variations, correspondence and financial data) to identify key details and metrics used to develop expert reports;
* Assisting in analysis or preparation of valuations and the processing and use of big data;
* Managing the workload and tasks of the project team;
* Managing budgets and fee reports;
* Dealing with clients and lawyers and interfacing as appropriate;
* Reviewing documentation (e.g. drawings, specifications, reports, estimates, variations, correspondence and financial data) to develop robust appendices.

**Requirements**
The successful candidate is likely to possess the following or similar qualifications:



* Bachelor’s degree in building construction, engineering, quantity surveying or related field;
* 5-10 years’ experience in a relevant field of quantity surveying, cost engineering, contracts management, construction management;
* Prior experience of working with Expert Witnesses;
* Strong software skills: MS Office Suite (especially Word & Excel), CostX / BIM / Buildsoft / Expert Estimation or similar;
* Experience in the preparation of first principles construction cost estimates;
* Experience in writing or contributing to Quantum Expert reports;
* Familiarity with construction cost management;
* Excellent written and verbal skills;
* Proficient with Microsoft Excel and comfortable with large sets of data;
* Able to adapt to a dynamic consultancy environment;
* Able to develop creative approaches and solutions necessary to resolve complex problems;
* A team player;
* English language (written and spoken), other languages an advantage;
* Able to meet tight deadlines and work under pressure;
* Excellent communication and presentation skills;
* Willing to occasionally travel domestically and internationally.

Secretariat is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We offer competitive compensation and benefits, and we support the continuing professional development of our employees.


A rewarding career above all


There are a lot of fine consulting firms out there. But when everything is on the line, it takes a unique combination of skill and savvy to succeed under pressure.


Our culture and people are driven by passion, pride, and performance. Passion for the clients we serve, the work we deliver, and the communities we live in. Pride in our cohesive team recognized for excellence and trusted to perform in the most challenging situations. And our track record of outstanding performance across all of our disciplines speaks for itself.


Our people are motivated to be the best in everything they do – from our approach to making the complex simple to the way we mentor our up-and-coming talent to become trusted experts early in their careers.


To learn how Secretariat collects, uses, and protects your personal information during the recruitment process, please review our Privacy Policy
